  "summary": "A traditional Finnish knotted pile rug featuring distinctive patterns and long, shaggy pile used as decorative textiles.",
  "description": "Ryijy rugs are characterized by their thick, shaggy pile and bold geometric or floral patterns in red, blue, yellow, and green. They originated in Finland as practical bed coverings and wall hangings, evolving from simple designs to elaborate folk art pieces that reflect Finnish cultural identity and seasonal traditions.",
